                  <provenance cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_102">Cambridge, Cambridgeshire.
                        King's College (Collegium regale Beate Marie et Sancti Nicholai)</orgName><p>At the end of the text is written ‘Finis decem librorum
                        Ethicorum Aristotelis secundum nouam translationem. Quod Hacumblen.’ (per
                        James, King’s, 20). The commentary is ascribed to Hacumblen’s authorship by
                        James and Tanner ‘but it is more likely that he simply copied the
                        manuscript’ (CBMLC 10, 697 citing Sharpe, Latin Writers, 552). Hacumblen
                        bequeathed ‘all my chieff books’ to King’s, of which this was perhaps one
                        (CBMLC 10, 697).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Perhaps Robert Hacumblen (d. 1528), fellow
                     and provost of King’s</provenance>
               </history>
